doc:sec-6-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6(2) Constitution of the Australian Federal Police" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of the finance law (within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013): (a) the Australian Federal Police is a listed entity; and (b) the Commissioner of Police is the accountable authority of the Australian Federal Police; and (c) the persons referred to in subsection (1) are officials of the Australian Federal Police; and (d) the purposes of the Australian Federal Police include the functions of the Australian Federal Police referred to in section 8." ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-8-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 Functions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-8-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The functions of the Australian Federal Police are: (a) subject to subsection (1A), the provision of police services in relation to the Australian Capital Territory; and (aa) the provision of police services in relation to the Jervis Bay Territory; and (b) the provision of police services in relation to:   Constitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II Constitution, functions and laws conferring powers on members etc.  Division 1 Section 8 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (i) laws of the Commonwealth; (ii) property of the Commonwealth (including Commonwealth places) and property of authorities of the Commonwealth; and (iii) the safeguarding of Commonwealth interests; and (baa) the investigation of State offences that have a federal aspect; and (ba) the provision of services in accordance with arrangements entered into under subsection (1C) and doing anything else included in the arrangements that is incidental or conducive to the provision of the services; and (bb) to perform the functions conferred by the Witness Protection Act 1994; and (bc) to perform the functions conferred by a law of a State or Territory that is a complementary witness protection law for the purposes of the Witness Protection Act 1994; and (bd) to perform functions under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002; and (be) to perform such protective and custodial functions as the Minister directs by notice in writing in the Gazette, being functions that relate to a person, matter or thing with respect to which the Parliament has legislative power; and (bf) the provision of police services and police support services for the purposes of assisting, or cooperating with, an Australian or foreign: (i) law enforcement agency; or (ii) intelligence or security agency; or (iii) government regulatory agency; and (bg) the provision of police services and police support services in relation to establishing, developing and monitoring peace, stability and security in foreign countries; and (bh) to assist or cooperate with: (i) an international organisation; or (ii) a non-governmental organisation, in relation to acts, omissions, matters or things outside Australia;" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The functions of the Australian Federal Police are: (a) subject to subsection (1A), the provision of police services in relation to the Australian Capital Territory; and (aa) the provision of police services in relation to the Jervis Bay Territory; and (b) the provision of police services in relation to:   Constitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II Constitution, functions and laws conferring powers on members etc.  Division 1 Section 8 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (i) laws of the Commonwealth; (ii) property of the Commonwealth (including Commonwealth places) and property of authorities of the Commonwealth; and (iii) the safeguarding of Commonwealth interests; and (baa) the investigation of State offences that have a federal aspect; and (ba) the provision of services in accordance with arrangements entered into under subsection (1C) and doing anything else included in the arrangements that is incidental or conducive to the provision of the services; and (bb) to perform the functions conferred by the Witness Protection Act 1994; and (bc) to perform the functions conferred by a law of a State or Territory that is a complementary witness protection law for the purposes of the Witness Protection Act 1994; and (bd) to perform functions under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002; and (be) to perform such protective and custodial functions as the Minister directs by notice in writing in the Gazette, being functions that relate to a person, matter or thing with respect to which the Parliament has legislative power; and (bf) the provision of police services and police support services for the purposes of assisting, or cooperating with, an Australian or foreign: (i) law enforcement agency; or (ii) intelligence or security agency; or (iii) government regulatory agency; and (bg) the provision of police services and police support services in relation to establishing, developing and monitoring peace, stability and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "caeff11367e90e4a3ddeb1cfa49ef8b75d53bf33db51ee6c55781c4ffbe13215" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Provision of police services in relation to various matters" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
