concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11 State and Territory writs and warrants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-11 ;
    values:originalText "Where a writ or warrant is issued under the law of a State or Territory in relation to an offence or other matter under a law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory, the writ or warrant may be executed by a member, notwithstanding that it is not addressed to a member and notwithstanding any requirement of the law of the State or Territory as to the person by whom it may be executed." ;
    skos:definition "Where a writ or warrant is issued under the law of a State or Territory in relation to an offence or other matter under a law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory, the writ or warrant may be executed by a member, notwithstanding that it is not addressed to a member and notwithstanding any requirement of the law of the State or Territory as to the person by whom it may be executed."@en ;
