doc:sec-12a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "12A(2) Immunity from State and Territory laws in relation to entry" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Where an AFP dog handler is entitled to enter, or to be on or in, particular premises or a particular place in the performance of the AFP dog handler’s duties as a member or a protective service officer, the AFP dog handler is entitled, in entering, or being on or in, the premises or place, to be accompanied by an AFP dog under the control of the AFP dog handler." ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-12a-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12A(3) Immunity from State and Territory laws in relation to entry"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-12a-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Commonwealth, a member or a protective service officer is not subject to any penalty, liability or forfeiture by reason only of an AFP dog having entered, or having been on or in, particular premises or a particular place if: (a) the AFP dog is under the control of an AFP dog handler;   Constitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II Constitution, functions and laws conferring powers on members etc.  Division 1 Section 12A Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (b) the AFP dog handler is performing the AFP dog handler’s duties as a member or protective service officer; and (c) the AFP dog handler is entitled to enter, or to be on or in, the premises or place." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The Commonwealth, a member or a protective service officer is not subject to any penalty, liability or forfeiture by reason only of an AFP dog having entered, or having been on or in, particular premises or a particular place if: (a) the AFP dog is under the control of an AFP dog handler;   Constitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II Constitution, functions and laws conferring powers on members etc.  Division 1 Section 12A Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (b) the AFP dog handler is performing the AFP dog handler’s duties as a member or protective service officer; and (c) the AFP dog handler is entitled to enter, or to be on or in, the premises or place."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8ccbeb9ab6cfc00ce77442d19f50cb3a758e5f754f1839f3b6805c09ef6b9dad" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-12a ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Commonwealth is not subject to penalty, liability or forfeiture for an AFP dog entering premises if under control of handler performing duties." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
