    cml:premiseText "Protective service officer must not cause death or grievous bodily harm unless necessary to protect life or prevent serious injury." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The protective service officer has an obligation to protect life and prevent serious injury." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14a-ss-2 cml:asserts concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14a-ss-2-logic-argumentation-5 .
concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14a-ss-2-logic-argumentation-5 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Argumentation ;
    cml:operator "Justification" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Justification for the prohibition" ;
    cml:premiseText "Protective service officer must not cause death or grievous bodily harm unless necessary to protect life or prevent serious injury." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The justification is that the protective service officer has a duty to protect life and prevent serious injury." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::argumentation" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-14a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "14A(2) Powers of arrest" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), a protective service officer must not, in arresting or attempting to arrest a person for an offence or in preventing a person who has been arrested for an offence from escaping, do an act likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm to the person unless the officer believes on reasonable grounds that the doing of the act is   Constitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II Powers and duties of protective service officers  Division 3 Section 14C Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 necessary to protect life or prevent serious injury to the officer or any other person." ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14C Arrested person to be informed of grounds of arrest"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-14c ;
    values:originalText "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence must inform the person, at the time of the arrest, of the offence for which the person is arrested. (2) It is sufficient compliance with subsection (1) if the protective service officer informs the person of the substance of the offence, and it is not necessary to do so in language of a precise or technical nature. (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the arrest by a protective service officer of a person for an offence if the person, by his or her own actions, makes it impracticable for the protective service officer to inform the person of the offence. (4) Where a protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence believes or has reasonable grounds for believing that the person is unable, by reason of inadequate knowledge of the English language or any physical or mental disability, to understand the substance of the offence for which the person is arrested, the protective service officer must, as soon as practicable, take all reasonable steps to ensure that the person is provided with an explanation of the substance of the offence that the person is able to understand." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence must inform the person, at the time of the arrest, of the offence for which the person is arrested. (2) It is sufficient compliance with subsection (1) if the protective service officer informs the person of the substance of the offence, and it is not necessary to do so in language of a precise or technical nature. (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the arrest by a protective service officer of a person for an offence if the person, by his or her own actions, makes it impracticable for the protective service officer to inform the person of the offence. (4) Where a protective service officer who arrests a person for an offence believes or has reasonable grounds for believing that the person is unable, by reason of inadequate knowledge of the English language or any physical or mental disability, to understand the substance of the offence for which the person is arrested, the protective service officer must, as soon as practicable, take all reasonable steps to ensure that the person is provided with an explanation of the substance of the offence that the person is able to understand."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "12c50d01fe41bf7d07dd2a9dc3279857d4dc3cd09df72c74ab76321dd11522b8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14c-ss-2 ;
