concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14g-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14G(4) Relationship of Division to other laws"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-14g-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Subject to subsection (2), the powers conferred, and duties imposed, by this Division on protective service officers are in   Constitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II Powers and duties of protective service officers  Division 3 Section 14G Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 addition to, and not in derogation of, any other powers conferred, or duties imposed, by any other law of the Commonwealth or the law of a State or Territory, and this Division is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth or the law of a State or Territory providing for such powers or duties in so far as it is capable of operating concurrently with this Division." ;
    skos:definition "(4) Subject to subsection (2), the powers conferred, and duties imposed, by this Division on protective service officers are in   Constitution, functions and powers of the Australian Federal Police  Part II Powers and duties of protective service officers  Division 3 Section 14G Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 addition to, and not in derogation of, any other powers conferred, or duties imposed, by any other law of the Commonwealth or the law of a State or Territory, and this Division is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any other law of the Commonwealth or the law of a State or Territory providing for such powers or duties in so far as it is capable of operating concurrently with this Division."@en ;
