concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-14g-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14G(5) Relationship of Division to other laws"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-14g-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) This Division, in so far as it protects the individual, is in addition to, and not in derogation of, any rights and freedoms of the individual, whether under the law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory, and this Division is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory providing for those rights and freedoms in so far as it is capable of operating concurrently with this Division." ;
    skos:definition "(5) This Division, in so far as it protects the individual, is in addition to, and not in derogation of, any rights and freedoms of the individual, whether under the law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory, and this Division is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory providing for those rights and freedoms in so far as it is capable of operating concurrently with this Division."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6617c01d1338612e41883d41d47c1761ea78b9f99584e5950f6e4974df5df949" ;
