concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-24 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24 Engagement of AFP employees"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-24 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner, on behalf of the Commonwealth, may, by writing, engage persons as employees. Engagement may be made subject to conditions (2) The engagement of an AFP employee may be made subject to conditions notified to the employee, including conditions dealing with any of the following matters: (a) probation; (b) citizenship; (c) formal qualifications; (d) security and character clearances; (e) health clearances; (f) secrecy requirements. (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the conditions that may be applied to the engagement of an AFP employee.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 25 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 Non-Australian citizen (4) The Commissioner must not engage, as an AFP employee, a person who is not an Australian citizen, unless the Commissioner considers it appropriate to do so. This section has no application to overseas engagement (5) This section does not apply to the engagement of persons overseas to perform duties overseas as employees. Note: Section 69A deals with the engagement of such persons." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner, on behalf of the Commonwealth, may, by writing, engage persons as employees. Engagement may be made subject to conditions (2) The engagement of an AFP employee may be made subject to conditions notified to the employee, including conditions dealing with any of the following matters: (a) probation; (b) citizenship; (c) formal qualifications; (d) security and character clearances; (e) health clearances; (f) secrecy requirements. (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the conditions that may be applied to the engagement of an AFP employee.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 25 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 Non-Australian citizen (4) The Commissioner must not engage, as an AFP employee, a person who is not an Australian citizen, unless the Commissioner considers it appropriate to do so. This section has no application to overseas engagement (5) This section does not apply to the engagement of persons overseas to perform duties overseas as employees. Note: Section 69A deals with the engagement of such persons."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2ba15729d2c7051dec7ec8b8f0baa67c52225ec53153e64506e9a9e059a87a7b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-24-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-24-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-24-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-24-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-24-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.58" .
doc:sec-24 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "24 Engagement of AFP employees" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner, on behalf of the Commonwealth, may, by writing, engage persons as employees. Engagement may be made subject to conditions (2) The engagement of an AFP employee may be made subject to conditions notified to the employee, including conditions dealing with any of the following matters: (a) probation; (b) citizenship; (c) formal qualifications; (d) security and character clearances; (e) health clearances; (f) secrecy requirements. (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the conditions that may be applied to the engagement of an AFP employee.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 25 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 Non-Australian citizen (4) The Commissioner must not engage, as an AFP employee, a person who is not an Australian citizen, unless the Commissioner considers it appropriate to do so. This section has no application to overseas engagement (5) This section does not apply to the engagement of persons overseas to perform duties overseas as employees. Note: Section 69A deals with the engagement of such persons." ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer .

