    cof:title "32(1) Retirement on invalidity grounds" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Commissioner is satisfied that an AFP employee should be retired because of physical or mental incapacity, the Commissioner may retire the employee by notice in writing given to the employee. AFP employee consents to retirement" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32(2) Retirement on invalidity grounds"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Before the Commissioner retires an AFP employee under subsection (1), the employee may, by notice in writing given to the Commissioner, consent to the Commissioner retiring the employee under that subsection. Note: To find out when an AFP employee’s retirement takes effect in such a case, see section 33.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 32 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 AFP employee not re-engaged because of invalidity" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Before the Commissioner retires an AFP employee under subsection (1), the employee may, by notice in writing given to the Commissioner, consent to the Commissioner retiring the employee under that subsection. Note: To find out when an AFP employee’s retirement takes effect in such a case, see section 33.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 32 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 AFP employee not re-engaged because of invalidity"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "efa0c383587e6c9d6d9625caa1b30f4a9ee8ab828b4e40964e4fe37975455adb" ;
