doc:sec-32-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32(2) Retirement on invalidity grounds" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Before the Commissioner retires an AFP employee under subsection (1), the employee may, by notice in writing given to the Commissioner, consent to the Commissioner retiring the employee under that subsection. Note: To find out when an AFP employee’s retirement takes effect in such a case, see section 33.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 32 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 AFP employee not re-engaged because of invalidity" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32(3) Retirement on invalidity grounds"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for a period; and (b) the person completes that period of engagement (the initial period); and (c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further period starting immediately after the end of the initial period; and (d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s physical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the person was not so re-engaged; the person is taken, for the purposes of the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988, the Superannuation Act and the Superannuation Act 2005, to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended. AFP employee is an eligible employee under the Superannuation Act 1976" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If: (a) a person is engaged as an AFP employee under section 24 for a period; and (b) the person completes that period of engagement (the initial period); and (c) the person is not re-engaged under that section for a further period starting immediately after the end of the initial period; and (d) the Commissioner certifies in writing that the person’s physical or mental incapacity was the only reason why the person was not so re-engaged; the person is taken, for the purposes of the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988, the Superannuation Act and the Superannuation Act 2005, to have been retired under this section on the day on which the initial period ended. AFP employee is an eligible employee under the Superannuation Act 1976"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9af1041f96880129590fd80ee6aa039d87b31ba45c13c9b272dde5e19ee73fc8" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-32 ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Certification of incapacity is required for retirement on invalidity grounds." ;
    dc:description "Commissioner's certification" ;
