doc:sec-33-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "33(1) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an AFP employee has consented to being retired under subsection 32(1), the employee’s retirement takes effect on the day specified in the notice under that subsection. The day specified must not be before the day on which the notice is given to the employee. AFP employee does not consent to retirement" ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "33(2) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-33-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If an AFP employee who is retired under subsection 32(1) has not consented to being retired under that subsection: (a) the notice given to the employee under that subsection must inform the employee that the employee is entitled to apply, within the period, and in the manner, prescribed by the regulations, for review of the Commissioner’s decision to retire the employee; and (b) subject to the outcome of any such review, the employee’s retirement takes effect on a day specified in the notice.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 34 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If an AFP employee who is retired under subsection 32(1) has not consented to being retired under that subsection: (a) the notice given to the employee under that subsection must inform the employee that the employee is entitled to apply, within the period, and in the manner, prescribed by the regulations, for review of the Commissioner’s decision to retire the employee; and (b) subject to the outcome of any such review, the employee’s retirement takes effect on a day specified in the notice.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III AFP employees  Division 2 Section 34 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "df228aa13083802f58a46822c2c53973467204a4a64ff8d41dc351dd8757389e" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33 ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employee must be informed of right to review retirement decision." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.66" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-2-norm .
