doc:sec-33-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "33(4) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The regulations may make provision in relation to the review of decisions of the Commissioner to retire AFP employees under subsection 32(1), where the employees have not consented to being retired under that subsection, including: (a) the period within which, and the manner in which, AFP employees may apply for review of such decisions; and (b) the powers available to a person or body conducting such a review; and (c) if the regulations make provision for a person or body conducting such a review to make recommendations to the Commissioner—the Commissioner giving effect to such recommendations by confirming or revoking such decisions." ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "33(5) Time when retirement on invalidity grounds takes effect"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-33-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Despite section 25D of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, if regulations under subsection (4) make provision for a person or body conducting a review of decisions of a kind mentioned in that subsection to: (a) give written reasons for any decision the person or body makes in relation to such a review; and (b) give a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned; the regulations may also make provision in relation to: (c) the exclusion from that copy of any information of a medical or psychiatric nature that the person or body thinks may be prejudicial to the employee’s physical or mental health or well-being; and (d) the employee nominating a medical practitioner to receive that information." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Despite section 25D of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, if regulations under subsection (4) make provision for a person or body conducting a review of decisions of a kind mentioned in that subsection to: (a) give written reasons for any decision the person or body makes in relation to such a review; and (b) give a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned; the regulations may also make provision in relation to: (c) the exclusion from that copy of any information of a medical or psychiatric nature that the person or body thinks may be prejudicial to the employee’s physical or mental health or well-being; and (d) the employee nominating a medical practitioner to receive that information."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bf378c0661bc2a42cf00329edb1e76758e4451f55f17be10e7fd928d2834dcc8" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33 ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Regulations must provide written reasons for decisions and a copy of those reasons to the AFP employee concerned." ;
    dc:description "yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.66" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-33-ss-5-norm .
