concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-35a-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35A(5) Payments in special circumstances"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-35a-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a condition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the Commonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction. Note: Payments under this section must be made from money appropriated by the Parliament. Generally, a payment can be debited against the Australian Federal Police’s annual appropriation, providing that it relates to some matter that has arisen in the course of its administration.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III Undertakings and oaths or affirmations  Division 4 Section 36 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025" ;
    skos:definition "(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a condition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the Commonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction. Note: Payments under this section must be made from money appropriated by the Parliament. Generally, a payment can be debited against the Australian Federal Police’s annual appropriation, providing that it relates to some matter that has arisen in the course of its administration.   Commissioner, Deputy Commissioners and AFP employees etc.  Part III Undertakings and oaths or affirmations  Division 4 Section 36 Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025"@en ;
