concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-37-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "37(5) General administration and control"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-37-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) The Minister may, after obtaining and considering the advice of the Commissioner and of the Secretary, make an arrangement with the appropriate Minister of a State for the provision or development of common services and for the use of such common services by the Australian Federal Police and the Police Force of the State." ;
