concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40RC Commissioner may determine professional standards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40rc ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner may issue Commissioner’s orders under section 38 determining the professional standards to be complied with by AFP appointees. (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner may determine a professional standard by reference to the requirements specified in: (a) another Commissioner’s order; or (b) another document issued or made by the Commissioner in the exercise of the Commissioner’s powers under section 37. (3) Despite section 46AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, a document referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) may be a document: (a) as in force at a particular time; or (b) as in force from time to time. Subdivision C—Unit within Australian Federal Police to undertake professional standards functions" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner may issue Commissioner’s orders under section 38 determining the professional standards to be complied with by AFP appointees. (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Commissioner may determine a professional standard by reference to the requirements specified in: (a) another Commissioner’s order; or (b) another document issued or made by the Commissioner in the exercise of the Commissioner’s powers under section 37. (3) Despite section 46AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, a document referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) may be a document: (a) as in force at a particular time; or (b) as in force from time to time. Subdivision C—Unit within Australian Federal Police to undertake professional standards functions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9a0c9b1506779687c7d5a82e8fd8173c311defa90d972442e57db514f9ffb948" ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rc-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rc-ss-2 ;
