doc:sec-40rc-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "40RC(3) Commissioner may determine professional standards" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Despite section 46AA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, a document referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) may be a document: (a) as in force at a particular time; or (b) as in force from time to time. Subdivision C—Unit within Australian Federal Police to undertake professional standards functions" ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40RD Unit to be constituted"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40rd ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner must constitute, within the Australian Federal Police, a unit to undertake investigations of: (a) AFP conduct issues that are category 3 conduct issues; and (b) corruption issues that relate to conduct engaged in by AFP appointees. (2) The Commissioner may determine, from time to time, the name by which the unit is to be known. (3) The establishment of the unit is to be such as the Commissioner determines from time to time." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner must constitute, within the Australian Federal Police, a unit to undertake investigations of: (a) AFP conduct issues that are category 3 conduct issues; and (b) corruption issues that relate to conduct engaged in by AFP appointees. (2) The Commissioner may determine, from time to time, the name by which the unit is to be known. (3) The establishment of the unit is to be such as the Commissioner determines from time to time."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d2ed035a4880b4e195d545c59b65d425223d5d4193ddac0224ffc91b138d2ce2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer ;
