doc:sec-40rn a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "40RN Category 1 conduct" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under subsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be category 1 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are satisfied that: (a) conduct of that kind is inappropriate conduct that: (i) relates to minor management matters or customer service matters; or" ;
    cof:pageNumber "103"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ro a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40RO Category 2 conduct"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40ro ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under subsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be category 2 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are satisfied that: (a) conduct of that kind is: (i) minor misconduct by an AFP appointee; or (ii) inappropriate conduct that reveals unsatisfactory behaviour by an AFP appointee; or (b) conduct of that kind: (i) would otherwise be category 1 conduct; and (ii) warrants, because of its repeated nature, being treated as category 2 conduct for the purposes of this Act. (2) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman must also be satisfied that the conduct does not warrant being treated as category 3 conduct for the purposes of this Act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under subsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be category 2 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are satisfied that: (a) conduct of that kind is: (i) minor misconduct by an AFP appointee; or (ii) inappropriate conduct that reveals unsatisfactory behaviour by an AFP appointee; or (b) conduct of that kind: (i) would otherwise be category 1 conduct; and (ii) warrants, because of its repeated nature, being treated as category 2 conduct for the purposes of this Act. (2) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman must also be satisfied that the conduct does not warrant being treated as category 3 conduct for the purposes of this Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "efa8568fe7e71f2fda43e7b3b2d71876a0c60e81094054941ddd12615abefc26" ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ro-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40ro-ss-2 ;
