concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40rp a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40RP Category 3 conduct"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40rp ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under subsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be category 3 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are satisfied that: (a) conduct of that kind: (i) is serious misconduct by an AFP appointee; or (ii) raises the question whether termination action should be taken in relation to an AFP appointee; or (iii) involves a breach of the criminal law, or serious neglect of duty, by an AFP appointee; and (b) conduct of that kind does not raise a corruption issue.   Professional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V Preliminary  Division 1 Section 40RQ Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (2) Subparagraphs (1)(a)(ii) and (iii) do not limit subparagraph (1)(a)(i)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner and the Ombudsman may determine under subsection 40RM(1) that conduct of a particular kind is to be category 3 conduct for the purposes of this Act only if they are satisfied that: (a) conduct of that kind: (i) is serious misconduct by an AFP appointee; or (ii) raises the question whether termination action should be taken in relation to an AFP appointee; or (iii) involves a breach of the criminal law, or serious neglect of duty, by an AFP appointee; and (b) conduct of that kind does not raise a corruption issue.   Professional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V Preliminary  Division 1 Section 40RQ Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (2) Subparagraphs (1)(a)(ii) and (iii) do not limit subparagraph (1)(a)(i)."@en ;
