    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), remedial action in relation to the AFP appointee may include one or more of the following:   Professional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V Dealing with AFP conduct or practices issues  Division 3 Section 40TE Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (a) action taken to improve the AFP appointee’s behaviour; (b) structured changes to the AFP appointee’s employment; (c) the recording of adverse findings against the AFP appointee (whether for a particular period or permanently)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40td-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40TD(3) Remedial action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40td-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Without limiting paragraph (2)(a), remedial action in relation to the AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms: (a) counselling the AFP appointee or arranging for the AFP appointee to be counselled; (b) reprimanding the AFP appointee; (c) giving the AFP appointee a formal warning; (d) requiring the AFP appointee to adopt particular improvement strategies." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Without limiting paragraph (2)(a), remedial action in relation to the AFP appointee may take one or more of the following forms: (a) counselling the AFP appointee or arranging for the AFP appointee to be counselled; (b) reprimanding the AFP appointee; (c) giving the AFP appointee a formal warning; (d) requiring the AFP appointee to adopt particular improvement strategies."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f247960264e522cc723d55ad178a7f8db98900628208a4aa3f234cac8542c5ba" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40td ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Remedial action may include counselling, reprimanding, or giving a formal warning to the AFP appointee." ;
