concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40tq a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40TQ How category 3 conduct issue or corruption issue is dealt with"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40tq ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if the issue is allocated to a person under section 40TN or 40TO. (2) In investigating the issue, the investigator must: (a) ensure that: (i) the AFP appointee; and (ii) the complainant (if any); have, subject to the requirements of the investigation, an adequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the issue; and (b) consider whether the information: (i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or (ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue; raises an AFP practices issue." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if the issue is allocated to a person under section 40TN or 40TO. (2) In investigating the issue, the investigator must: (a) ensure that: (i) the AFP appointee; and (ii) the complainant (if any); have, subject to the requirements of the investigation, an adequate opportunity to be heard in relation to the issue; and (b) consider whether the information: (i) given under section 40SA in relation to the issue; or (ii) obtained in the course of dealing with the issue; raises an AFP practices issue."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e4152c4b4a3c98f26908be25413469a9b40d029beb2c468596c1cdba6d0f7f4f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "122"^^xsd:integer ;
