doc:sec-40vb-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "40VB(3) Manner of conducting investigation or inquiry" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) the investigator is investigating a category 3 conduct issue or a corruption issue; and (b) the head of the unit constituted under section 40RD allocated the issue to the investigator; the head of that unit may give the investigator directions as to the manner in which the investigation is to be conducted and the investigator must comply with those directions." ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40vc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40VC Obtaining information and making inquiries"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40vc ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of the investigation or inquiry, the investigator may obtain information from such persons, and make such inquiries, as he or she thinks fit. (2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to this Division." ;
