concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40yb a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40YB Providing false information about AFP conduct or practices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-40yb ;
    values:originalText "issues A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) gives information under section 40SA that raises an AFP conduct or practices issue; or (ii) otherwise gives an AFP appointee information in relation to an AFP conduct or practices issue; and (b) the person knows that the information is false in a material particular. Penalty: 20 penalty units.   Professional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V Offences  Division 8 Section 40YC Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 40YC  AFP appointees to provide name, etc. An AFP appointee commits an offence if: (a) a person requests the AFP appointee to give the person any of the following: (i) his or her name; (ii) the address of his or her place of duty; (iii) his or her identification number if her or she has an identification number; and (b) the person informs the AFP appointee, either expressly or by necessary implication, that the person: (i) is complaining, or proposes to complain, about action taken by that AFP appointee; or (ii) is giving information, or proposed to give information, under section 40SA about an AFP conduct issue that relates to conduct engaged in by that AFP appointee; and (c) the AFP appointee: (i) refuses or fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with the request; or (ii) gives the person a name, address or identification number that is false in a material particular. Penalty: 5 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "issues A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) gives information under section 40SA that raises an AFP conduct or practices issue; or (ii) otherwise gives an AFP appointee information in relation to an AFP conduct or practices issue; and (b) the person knows that the information is false in a material particular. Penalty: 20 penalty units.   Professional standards and AFP conduct and practices issues  Part V Offences  Division 8 Section 40YC Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 40YC  AFP appointees to provide name, etc. An AFP appointee commits an offence if: (a) a person requests the AFP appointee to give the person any of the following: (i) his or her name; (ii) the address of his or her place of duty; (iii) his or her identification number if her or she has an identification number; and (b) the person informs the AFP appointee, either expressly or by necessary implication, that the person: (i) is complaining, or proposes to complain, about action taken by that AFP appointee; or (ii) is giving information, or proposed to give information, under section 40SA about an AFP conduct issue that relates to conduct engaged in by that AFP appointee; and (c) the AFP appointee: (i) refuses or fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with the request; or (ii) gives the person a name, address or identification number that is false in a material particular. Penalty: 5 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eda35e1d356dc1cf045d7ee80916ef3a52463e512f6252046457f7f3714e6af0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Providing false information about AFP conduct or practices" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.142" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-40yb-norm .
