concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-43 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "43 Notice of charge etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-43 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Where: (a) either: (i) a person who is or was an AFP employee is charged with an offence; or (ii) a person who was an old law member or staff member at any time is charged with an offence; and (b) the Commissioner considers that the offence is, or may be, a corruption offence; the Commissioner shall notify the Minister administering the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 in writing of the charge. (2) A notice shall contain particulars of the charge and set out the reasons why the Commissioner considers that the offence is, or may be, a corruption offence. (3) Where the Commissioner notifies the Minister administering the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 that a person has been charged with an offence, the Commissioner shall notify that Minister in writing if: (a) the person is acquitted or convicted of the offence; or (b) the charge is withdrawn or otherwise disposed of without the conviction of the person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Where: (a) either: (i) a person who is or was an AFP employee is charged with an offence; or (ii) a person who was an old law member or staff member at any time is charged with an offence; and (b) the Commissioner considers that the offence is, or may be, a corruption offence; the Commissioner shall notify the Minister administering the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 in writing of the charge. (2) A notice shall contain particulars of the charge and set out the reasons why the Commissioner considers that the offence is, or may be, a corruption offence. (3) Where the Commissioner notifies the Minister administering the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 that a person has been charged with an offence, the Commissioner shall notify that Minister in writing if: (a) the person is acquitted or convicted of the offence; or (b) the charge is withdrawn or otherwise disposed of without the conviction of the person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "53c1fe33bac3ae0d183bbe93f241d72b8953fa4292073a6b357a2e64b5a99f62" ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-43-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-43-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-43-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf, p.156" .
