specified day plus the amount of interest on those contributions accrued under the scheme before that day; is prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the certificate. (5) A document purporting to be sealed with the seal of a court is to be taken to have been lawfully sealed with the seal of that court unless the contrary is proved. (6) A document purporting to be signed or sealed by a person’s superannuation authority is to be taken to have been signed or duly sealed by that superannuation authority unless the contrary is proved." ;
