concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47(3) Effect of superannuation order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-47-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Despite the Superannuation Act, or any other Act or any agreement, where subsection (1) applies to a person: (a) who: (i) was an AFP employee at the time the relevant corruption offence was committed but was not such an employee when charged with that offence; or (ii) was an old law member or staff member at the time the relevant corruption offence was committed but was not such a member or an AFP employee when charged with that offence; and (b) who would, but for that subsection, have been entitled to payment of benefits under the relevant superannuation scheme on or after the day on which the superannuation order takes effect; the person is entitled, on the day on which he or she ceases to be a member of the scheme, to payment of an amount worked out using the formula: where: AC is an amount equal to the sum of the employee contributions paid under the scheme by the person plus the amount of interest on those contributions accrued under the scheme; and AC – AR" ;
    skos:definition "(3) Despite the Superannuation Act, or any other Act or any agreement, where subsection (1) applies to a person: (a) who: (i) was an AFP employee at the time the relevant corruption offence was committed but was not such an employee when charged with that offence; or (ii) was an old law member or staff member at the time the relevant corruption offence was committed but was not such a member or an AFP employee when charged with that offence; and (b) who would, but for that subsection, have been entitled to payment of benefits under the relevant superannuation scheme on or after the day on which the superannuation order takes effect; the person is entitled, on the day on which he or she ceases to be a member of the scheme, to payment of an amount worked out using the formula: where: AC is an amount equal to the sum of the employee contributions paid under the scheme by the person plus the amount of interest on those contributions accrued under the scheme; and AC – AR"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b0665f536997e7133d8f7bd29d7ab1667f0bbb1cbf36de9abc914d648651388e" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-47 ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Entitlement to payment of benefits upon cessation of membership" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-federal-police-act-1979.pdf> ;
