concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-51-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "51(3) Person ceases to be an AFP employee: persons charged with"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-51-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Where the Commissioner notifies a superannuation authority that the rights and entitlements of a person are suspended: (a) the person is entitled, on the day on which he or she ceases to be an AFP employee, to receive payment, if the person elects to do so, of an amount equal to the sum of the employee contributions paid under the scheme by the person (being contributions held in a fund under the scheme) plus the amount of interest on those contributions accrued under the scheme; and (b) the person is not entitled to exercise any other right, or to receive any other benefit, under the scheme, or to receive an adjustment payment, unless: (i) the person is acquitted of the offence or the charge is withdrawn or otherwise disposed of without the conviction of the person;   Loss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA Miscellaneous  Division 4 Section 53A Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (ii) the person is convicted of the offence, but does not receive a sentence that would support the making of an application for a superannuation order under subsection 45(1A); (iii) the Minister administering the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 refuses to authorise the DPP to apply for a superannuation order in respect of the person; (iv) the appropriate court refuses to make a superannuation order in respect of the person; or (v) a superannuation order made in respect of the person is taken to have been revoked." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Where the Commissioner notifies a superannuation authority that the rights and entitlements of a person are suspended: (a) the person is entitled, on the day on which he or she ceases to be an AFP employee, to receive payment, if the person elects to do so, of an amount equal to the sum of the employee contributions paid under the scheme by the person (being contributions held in a fund under the scheme) plus the amount of interest on those contributions accrued under the scheme; and (b) the person is not entitled to exercise any other right, or to receive any other benefit, under the scheme, or to receive an adjustment payment, unless: (i) the person is acquitted of the offence or the charge is withdrawn or otherwise disposed of without the conviction of the person;   Loss of certain superannuation rights and benefits  Part VA Miscellaneous  Division 4 Section 53A Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (ii) the person is convicted of the offence, but does not receive a sentence that would support the making of an application for a superannuation order under subsection 45(1A); (iii) the Minister administering the Crimes (Superannuation Benefits) Act 1989 refuses to authorise the DPP to apply for a superannuation order in respect of the person; (iv) the appropriate court refuses to make a superannuation order in respect of the person; or (v) a superannuation order made in respect of the person is taken to have been revoked."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "26269b6f6c471d9f7d47e586ad2a4343e5f2ee169249d90166177c3d11d29cac" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-51 ;
    cof:pageNumber "178"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Person entitled to receive payment upon ceasing employment if certain conditions met." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
