doc:sec-64a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "64A(2) Members in uniform to wear identification numbers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code." ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64a-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "64A(3) Members in uniform to wear identification numbers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-64a-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1) if the defendant proves that his or her identification number was not clearly visible on the uniform as a consequence of: (a) the act of another person (not being a protective service officer) done without the consent of the defendant; or   Miscellaneous  Part VI  Section 64AA Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (b) an unintentional omission of the defendant. Note: The defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in subsection (3). See section 13.4 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(3) It is a defence to a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1) if the defendant proves that his or her identification number was not clearly visible on the uniform as a consequence of: (a) the act of another person (not being a protective service officer) done without the consent of the defendant; or   Miscellaneous  Part VI  Section 64AA Australian Federal Police Act 1979 Compilation date: 08/11/2025 (b) an unintentional omission of the defendant. Note: The defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in subsection (3). See section 13.4 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0322f578505e3f00324756cdb29db31ecd5081072dd06f928ae7ae6236a04ef4" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-act-1979-sec-64a ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defence against prosecution for offence under subsection (1) The Commissioner must take steps to enable members to comply with subsection (1)." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
